---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CodeExample from "../../components/CodeExample.astro";
import PageIntro from "../../components/PageIntro.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../consts";
import lessonSource from "../../generated/examples/tutorial-loops.kwe?raw";

const source = lessonSource.trimEnd();
const output = "Mgbe\n1\n2\n3\nKwụsị\n1\nGaa n'ihu\n1\n3\n4";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Lesson 4: Repetition and Loop Control"
  description="Learn Kwechiri mgbe loops, early exit with kwụsị, and continuation with gaa n'ihu."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Tutorial 04"
    title="Repetition and Loop Control"
    lead="Repeat statements while a Boolean condition is true, stop a loop early, and skip to its next iteration."
    meta="Beginner · Complete Lesson 3 first"
  />

  <div class="shell content-layout">
    <nav class="docs-nav" aria-label="Tutorial navigation">
      <a href="/tutorials/expressions-and-decisions/">← Lesson 3: Expressions and Decisions</a>
      <a href="/tutorials/repetition-and-loop-control/" aria-current="page">Lesson 4: Repetition and loop control</a>
      <span>Functions · Planned</span>
      <span>Collections · Planned</span>
    </nav>
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>The program</h2>
      <p>Open <code>examples/tutorials/loops.kwe</code>.</p>
      <CodeExample label="examples/tutorials/loops.kwe" code={source} output={output} />

      <h2>Run it</h2>
      <pre><code>node dist/cli/index.js examples/tutorials/loops.kwe</code></pre>

      <h2><code>mgbe</code></h2>
      <p><code>mgbe</code> checks its Boolean condition before every iteration:</p>
      <pre><code>mgbe (onụọgụ &lt;= 3) &#123;
    bipụta(onụọgụ)
    onụọgụ = onụọgụ + 1
&#125;</code></pre>
      <p>
        The condition can be false immediately, so a loop may run zero times.
        Update loop-carried variables so the condition can eventually become
        false; otherwise the loop may continue forever.
      </p>

      <h2><code>kwụsị</code></h2>
      <p><code>kwụsị</code> exits the nearest enclosing loop:</p>
      <pre><code>ọ bụrụ (onụọgụ == 2) &#123;
    kwụsị
&#125;</code></pre>
      <p>
        The statements after the conditional remain valid, but on the iteration
        where the branch runs, the loop ends before reaching them.
      </p>

      <h2><code>gaa n'ihu</code></h2>
      <p><code>gaa n'ihu</code> starts the next iteration of the nearest loop:</p>
      <pre><code>ọ bụrụ (onụọgụ == 2) &#123;
    gaa n'ihu
&#125;
bipụta(onụọgụ)</code></pre>
      <p>
        When <code>onụọgụ</code> is <code>2</code>, the print is skipped and the
        loop begins its next iteration with <code>onụọgụ</code> equal to
        <code>3</code>.
      </p>

      <h2>Nearest loop</h2>
      <p>
        Both statements target the nearest enclosing loop. In nested loops they
        do not target an outer loop. <code>kwụsị</code> exits only the loop, not
        the whole function. <code>laghachi</code> is the statement that exits a
        function.
      </p>

      <h2>Your turn</h2>
      <p>
        Change the <code>kwụsị</code> condition to
        <code>onụọgụ == 4</code> and predict how the output changes. Then remove
        <code>onụọgụ = onụọgụ + 1</code> from the first loop and explain why the
        program no longer finishes.
      </p>

      <div class="callout callout--gold">
        <strong>Common problems</strong>
        Loop conditions must be Boolean. Use <code>kwụsị</code> only inside a
        loop to stop it, and <code>gaa n'ihu</code> only inside a loop to skip
        to the next iteration. Neither statement affects an outer loop.
      </div>

      <h2>Normative references</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href={`${SITE.github}/blob/main/docs/language-spec/control-flow.md`}>Control flow</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${SITE.github}/blob/main/docs/language-spec/variables.md`}>Variables</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${SITE.github}/blob/main/docs/language-spec/errors.md`}>Current language errors</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Next</h2>
      <p>Lesson 5 will introduce <code>ọrụ</code> functions, parameters, calls, and <code>laghachi</code>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
